  {
    "sha": "24aee9e73918e995886bb6e158dbd0cecee6237c",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVouz_toAKDI0YWVlOWU3MzkxOGU5OTU4ODZiYjZlMTU4ZGJkMGNlY2VlNjIzN2M",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T14:59:29Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T14:59:29Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(tools): a refused tool names itself and the rule it breaks\n\nThe project loader refused a tool with unusable numbers as \"tool\nparameters are not usable: ToolDto { ... }\", a debug dump that named\nneither the tool nor the field. AddTool, ChangeTool, the library import\nand the library reader printed the same dump or a generic line.\n\nNew Tool::why_not_sane() (tools::tool_sanity) returns the first rule\nbroken, in plain words, for example \"turning surface speed 0 m/min is\noutside 0..2000 m/min (it must be over 0)\". Tool::is_sane and\nTurningData::is_sane are now why_not_sane().is_none(), so the words and\nthe verdict cannot drift apart. All four refusals now read\n\"tool '<name>': <rule>\".\n\nThe old is_sane bodies are kept verbatim in the tests as an oracle and\nswept against the new law: every catalog tool as each kind, 13 fields x\n13 edge values, flutes, orientation and turning data. The verdict is\nunchanged everywhere.\n\nFixes #1186\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
